#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Pitanja i Odgovori"

#. Tag: chapter
#: faq.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "&reporting.bugs; &updating.documentation;"
msgstr "&reporting.bugs; &updating.documentation;"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is the &kstars; Icon?"
msgstr "Sta je &kstar; Ikona?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guiicon>&kstars; Icon</guiicon> is a sextant, a handheld telescope "
"which was used by navigators on sailing ships back when the stars were "
"important for navigation. By carefully reckoning the positions of the stars, "
"the navigator could get an accurate estimate of the ship's current <link "
"linkend=\"ai-geocoords\">longitude and latitude</link>."
msgstr ""
"<guiicon> &kstars; Ikona </guiicon> je sekstant, ručni teleskop koji je "
"korišten od strane nautičare na jedrenjacima unatrag kada su zvijezde bile "
"važne za plovidbu. Pažljivim obračun pozicije zvijezda, navigator mogao "
"dobiti točnu procjenu broda trenutne <link linkend = \"Ai-geocoords\"> "
"dužina i širina </link>."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "What do the different symbols for deep-sky objects mean?"
msgstr "Što različiti simboli za objekte u dubokom nebu znače?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "The symbol indicates the object type:"
msgstr "Simbol označava vrstu objekta:"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "dotted circle: Open Cluster"
msgstr "tačkasti krug: Otvori klaster"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid "cross-in-circle: Globular Cluster"
msgstr "krug sa plusom: Loptasti Klaster"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "box: Gaseous Nebula"
msgstr "kutija: Gaseous Nebula"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "diamond: Supernova Remnant"
msgstr "dijamant: Supernova Ostatak"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "circle with outer lines: Planetary Nebula"
msgstr "krug s vanjskim linijama: Planetarna Maglica"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "ellipse: Galaxy"
msgstr "elipsa: Galaksija"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "What do the different colors of Deep-sky objects mean?"
msgstr "Sta znace razlicite boje od Objekata daleko u nebu?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Generally, the different colors indicate to which catalog the object belongs "
"(Messier, NGC or IC). However, some objects have a different color which "
"indicates that there are extra images available in the <link linkend=\"popup-"
"menu\">popup menu</link> (the default <quote>extras</quote> color is red)."
msgstr ""
"Općenito, različiti boje ukazuju na koje Katalog predmet pripada (Messier, "
"NGC ili IC). Međutim, neki predmeti imaju različite boje koje ukazuju na to "
"da postoje dodatni slike dostupne u <link linkend=\"popup-menu\">popup "
"meniu</link> (zadana <quote>ekstra </quote> boja je crvena)."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why are there so many more U.S. cities than in other countries?"
msgstr "Zašto ima toliko mnogo više U.S.  gradova nego u drugim zemljama?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When we started &kstars;, we were unable to find a longitude/latitude "
"database that covered the globe equitably. However, the &kstars; community "
"is rapidly overcoming this problem! We have already received city lists from "
"many users around the world. If you can contribute to this effort, please "
"send us your list of cities and coordinates."
msgstr ""
"Kad smo počeli i &kstars;, nismo mogli naći dužine / širine baze podataka "
"koja pokriva svijet ravnomjerno. Međutim, i &kstars; Zajednicaje nasla "
"rjesnje za  brzo prevladavanje ovog problema! Već smo dobili popise grad od "
"mnogih korisnika širom svijeta. Ako možete doprinijeti ovom nastojanju, "
"pošaljite nam svoj popis gradova i koordinata."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have added a custom location to &kstars; that I no longer want. How do I "
"remove it from the program?"
msgstr ""
"Ja sam dodao proizvoljno mjesto na &kstars; koje ja više ne želim. Kako da "
"ga izbacim iz programa?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will have to edit the <filename>~/.kde/share/apps/kstars/mycities.dat</"
"filename> file, and remove the location's line from that file."
msgstr ""
"Morat cete promijeniti  <filename>~/.kde/share/apps/kstars/mycities.dat</"
"filename> fajl, i izbaciti linije za lokaciju iz fajla."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why can I not display the ground when using Equatorial Coordinates?"
msgstr ""
"Zašto se ne mogu prikazati na zemlju prilikom korištenja ekvatorijalnih "
"koordinata?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The short answer is, this is a temporary limitation. There is a problem when "
"constructing the filled polygon that represents the ground when in "
"Equatorial mode. However, it does not make too much sense to draw the ground "
"in equatorial coordinates, which is why this fix has been given a low "
"priority."
msgstr ""
"Kratak odgovor glasi, to je privremeno ograničenje. Došlo je do problema "
"prilikom izgradnje ispunjenog poligona koji predstavlja zemlju kada u "
"Ekvatorijalnoj modu. Međutim, to ne bi imalo previše smisla tj. crtanje "
"teren u Ekvatorijalnoj koordinatama, što je razlog zašto je riješenje toga "
"dobilo nizak prioritet."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why do some objects disappear when I am scrolling the display?"
msgstr "Zašto su neki predmeti nestaju kada skrolam ekranom?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the display is in motion, &kstars; must recompute the screen "
"coordinates of every object in its database, which involves some pretty "
"heavy trigonometry. When scrolling the display (either with the arrow keys "
"or by dragging with the mouse), the display may become slow and jerky, "
"because the computer is having trouble keeping up. By excluding many of the "
"objects, the computational load is greatly reduced, which allows for "
"smoother scrolling. You can turn off this feature in the <guilabel>Configure "
"&kstars;</guilabel> window, and you can also configure which objects get "
"hidden."
msgstr ""
"Kad je zaslon u pokretu, i &kstars; mora osvjeziti ekrana koordinate svakog "
"objekta u svojoj bazi podataka, koja uključuje neke prilično tešku "
"trigonometriju. Kada pomičete zaslon (ili sa strelicama ili povlačenjem "
"mišem), zaslon može postati spor i isprekidan, jer računalo ima problema "
"zadržati up. Isključivanjem mnogih objekata, računalna opterećenja znatno je "
"smanjen, što omogućuje glatko pomicanje. Možete isključiti ovu značajku u "
"<guilabel> Konfiguracija i &kstars; </guilabel> prozor, a možete podesiti "
"koji objekat ce biti skriven."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I do not understand all the terms used in &kstars;. Where can I learn more "
"about the astronomy behind the program?"
msgstr ""
"Ja ne razumijem sve pojmove koji se koriste u &kstars;. Gdje mogu saznati "
"više o astronomiji iz programa?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kstars; Handbook includes the <link linkend=\"astroinfo\">AstroInfo "
"Project</link>; a series of short, hyperlinked articles about astronomical "
"topics that can be explored and illustrated with &kstars;. AstroInfo is a "
"community effort, like GNUpedia or Everything2. If you'd like to contribute "
"to AstroInfo, please join our mailing list: <email>kstars-devel@kde.org</"
"email>."
msgstr ""
"&kstars; Priručnik obuhvaća <link linkend = \"astroinfo\"> AstroInfo Project "
"</link>;niz kratkih, hiperlinkovima članaka o astronomskim temama koje mogu "
"biti istražena i predstavljena i kstars;. AstroInfo je zajednica , kao što "
"su GNUpedia ili Everything2. Ako želite doprinijeti AstroInfo, pridružite "
"našoj mailing listu:  <email>kstars-devel@kde.org</email>."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I want &kstars; to start up with a time and date different from my system "
"CPU clock. Is this possible?"
msgstr ""
"Želim &kstars; da pocne s vremenom i datumom koji se razlikuje od mog "
"sistemskog CPU sata. Je li to moguće?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes; to start kstars with a different time/date, use the <quote>--date</"
"quote> argument, followed by a date string like <quote>4 July 1976 12:30:00</"
"quote>"
msgstr ""
"Da; za početak kstars s različitim vrijeme / datum, upotrijebite <quote>- -"
"datum </quote> argument, nakon čega slijedi datum niz poput <quote> 4. "
"srpanj 1976 00:30:00 </quote>"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I want &kstars; to start up with the simulation clock paused. Is this "
"possible?"
msgstr ""
"Zelim &kstars; da pocne sa simulacionim satom pauziranim. Da li je to moguce?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes; to start kstars with the clock paused, simply add the <quote>--paused</"
"quote> argument to the command line."
msgstr ""
"Da; da zapocnete kstars za puziranim satom, samo dodajte  <quote>--paused</"
"quote> argument na komandnu liniju."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "How accurate/precise is &kstars;?"
msgstr "Koliko je je ustvari tacan/precizan  &kstars;?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kstars; is pretty accurate, but it is not (yet) as precise as it can "
"possibly be. The problem with high-precision calculations is that you start "
"having to deal with a large number of complicating factors. If you are not a "
"professional astronomer, you will probably never have a problem with its "
"accuracy or precision."
msgstr ""
"&kstars; je prilično točno, ali to je (još) nije tako precizno kao što "
"eventualno može biti.Problem s visoke preciznosti izračuna je da počnete da "
"se bave velikim brojem kompliciranih faktora. Ako niste profesionalni "
"astronom, vi ćete vjerojatno nikada imati problema sa svojom točnošću i "
"preciznošću."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is a list of some of the complicating factors which limit the program's "
"precision:"
msgstr ""
"Ovdje je popis nekih od kompliciranih faktora koji ograničavaju preciznost "
"programa:"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Planet positions are only accurate for dates within 4000 years or so of the "
"current epoch. The planet positions are predicted using a Fourier-like "
"analysis of their orbits, as observed over the past few centuries. We learnt "
"in school that planets follow simple elliptical orbits around the Sun, but "
"this is not strictly true. It would be true only if there was only one "
"planet in the Solar system, and if the Sun and the planet were both point "
"masses. As it is, the planets are constantly tugging on each other, "
"perturbing the orbits slightly, and tidal effects also induce precessional "
"wobbling. In fact, recent analysis suggests that the planets' orbits may not "
"even be stable in the long term (i.e., millions or billions of years). As a "
"rule of thumb, you can expect the position of a planet to be accurate to a "
"few arcseconds between the dates -2000 and 6000."
msgstr ""
"Pozicije planta su samo točne unazad 4000 godina ili na taj način od "
"trenutne epohe. Pozicij planeta predviđa pomoću Fourier-poput analizu "
"njihovih putanja, kao promatrana tijekom posljednjih nekoliko stoljeća. "
"Naučili smo u školi da planeti slijede jednostavne eliptične orbite oko "
"Sunca, ali to je strogo rečeno nije istina. To bi bilo istinito samo ako "
"postoji samo jedan planet u Sunčevom sustavu, a ako Sunce i planet su obje "
"točke mase. Kao što je, planeti stalno vuče na svaki drugi, odskace od  "
"orbite malo, i plime  izazivaju odskakanje odorbite . Naime, nedavna analiza "
"sugerira da je planeta u orbiti ne može ni biti stabilan na dugi rok (tj "
"milijuna ili milijardi godina). Kao pravilo, možete očekivati položaj "
"planeta biti točni na nekoliko kutnih sekundi između 2000 i 6000."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pluto is the exception to this; its position is perhaps ten times less "
"precise than the positions of the other planets. Still, for dates near the "
"present epoch, its position can be trusted to about an arcsecond."
msgstr ""
"Pluton je iznimka; njegova pozicija je možda deset puta manje precizna od "
"pozicija drugih planeta. Ipak, za datume u blizini sadašnje epohe, njegova "
"pozicija se može vjerovati da je tačna s tolarancijom ugaone sekunde."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The moon's position is the most difficult to predict to high precision. This "
"is because its motion is quite perturbed by the Earth. Also, since it is so "
"nearby, even minute effects that would be undetectable in more distant "
"bodies are easily apparent in the moon."
msgstr ""
"Položaj Mjeseca je najteže predvidjeti da visoke preciznosti. To je zato što "
"njegovo kretanje vrlo ometen od Zemlje. Također, budući da je tako u "
"neposrednoj blizini, čak i minute uticu na to da bi neotkriveni objketkti "
"koji su dalji lakse pojave na mjesecu ."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The objects with the worst long-term precision in the program are the comets "
"and asteroids. We use a very simplistic orbital model for the minor planets "
"that does not include third-body perturbations. Therefore, their positions "
"can only be trusted for dates near the present epoch. Even for the present "
"epoch, one can expect positional errors among the minor planets of order 10 "
"arcseconds or more."
msgstr ""
"Predmeti s najgorim dugoročno preciznosti u programu su kometi i asteroidi. "
"Koristimo vrlo jednostavna orbitalnu modela za manje planete koje ne "
"uključuju treće tijelo poremećaje. Dakle, njihove pozicije mogu biti "
"pouzdane  samo za datume u blizini sadašnjeg doba. Čak i za sadašnje epohe, "
"može se očekivati položajne pogreške među manjim planetima reda 10 kutnih "
"sekundi ili više."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why do I have to download an improved NGC/IC catalog and Messier object "
"images? Why not just include them as part of the &kstars; distribution?"
msgstr ""
"Zašto ja moram preuzeti poboljšane NGC / IC kataloge i Messierov katalog "
"slike? Zašto ne samo uključiti ih kao dio &kstars; distribucije?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The author of the downloadable NGC/IC catalog has released it with the "
"restriction that it may not be used commercially. For most &kstars; users, "
"this is not a problem. However, it is technically against the &kstars; "
"license (the <acronym>GPL</acronym>) to restrict usage in this way. We "
"removed the Messier object images from the standard distribution for two "
"reasons: to simply reduce the size of &kstars;, and also because of similar "
"licensing concerns with a couple of the images. The inline images are "
"significantly compressed to a very low quality from their original form, so "
"I doubt there is a real copyright concern, but I did obtain explicit "
"permission from the images' authors to use the few images for which there "
"was any question about it (see <filename>README.images</filename>). Still, "
"just to be absolutely safe, I removed them from the standard distribution, "
"and marked the download archive as being \"free for non-commercial use\"."
msgstr ""
"Autor za preuzimanje NGC / IC katalogu je to objavio uz ograničenje da se ne "
"može koristiti u komercijalne svrhe. Za većinu &kstars; Korisnika, to nije "
"problem. Međutim, to je tehnički protiv &kstars; licenca (<acronym>GPL</"
"acronym>) će ograničiti korištenje na ovaj način. Uklonili smo Messier "
"objekata slike iz standardne distribucije iz dva razloga: kako bi se "
"jednostavno smanjiti veličinu &kstars;, i zbog sličnih problema licenciranja "
"s nekoliko slika .Ugrađene slike značajno komprimirane na vrlo nizak "
"kvalitet  prema izvornim obliku, tako da se sumnja da je pravi problem "
"autorskih prava, ali sam dobio izričito dopuštenje od autora slika 'da "
"koristi nekoliko slika za koje je bilo pitanje o tome (pogledajte <filename> "
"README.images </filename>). Ipak, samo da budem apsolutno siguran, ja sam ih "
"uklonio iz standardne distribucije, a obilježili su preuzimanje arhive kao "
"\"slobodan za nekomercijalnu upotrebu\"."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I am really enjoying the beautiful images I have downloaded through "
"&kstars;! I would like to share them with the world; can I publish a "
"calendar featuring these images (or are there any usage restrictions on the "
"images)?"
msgstr ""
"Ja sam stvarno uživao u prekrasnim slikama preuzetim putem &kstars;! Želim "
"ih podijeliti sa svijetom; mogu li objaviti kalendar koji sadrži ove slike "
"(ili postoje li ograničenja upotrebe slika)?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It depends on the image, but many of the images restrict against commercial "
"usage. The Image Viewer's statusbar will usually contain information about "
"the image's copyright holder, and what usage restrictions apply. As a rule "
"of thumb: anything published by NASA is in the public domain (including all "
"HST images). For everything else, you can pretty safely assume that the "
"images may not be used commercially without permission. When in doubt, "
"contact the image's copyright holder directly."
msgstr ""
"To ovisi o slici, ali mnoge od slika ograničavaju komercijalnu upotrebu."
"Statusna traka slike će obično sadržavati podatke o slici, ko je nositelj "
"autorskih prava, a koja ograničenja korištenja vrijede. Kao pravilo: sve što "
"je objavio NASA je u javnoj domeni (uključujući sve slike HST). Za sve "
"ostalo,  prilično sigurno se može pretpostaviti da se slike ne mogu se "
"stavljati na tržište bez dopuštenja. Kada ste u nedoumici, obratite se "
"izravno  nositelju autorskog prava na sliku."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I help contribute to future versions of &kstars;?"
msgstr "Mogu li vam pomoći doprinijeti budućim verzijama &kstars;?"

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes, definitely! Introduce yourself on our mailing list: <email>kstars-"
"devel@kde.org</email>. If you want to help with the coding, download the "
"latest <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Projects/Edu/KStars/"
"Building_KStars\">&kstars; Git</ulink> version of the code and dive right "
"in. There are several README files in the distribution that explain some of "
"the code's subsystems. If you need ideas of what to work on, see the TODO "
"file. You can submit patches to kstars-devel, and feel free to post any "
"questions you have about the code there as well."
msgstr ""
"Da, definitivno! Predstavite se na našu mailing listu: <email>kstars-"
"devel@kde.org</email>. Ako želite pomoći s kodiranje, preuzmite najnoviju "
"<ulink url = \"http://techbase.kde.org/Projects/Edu/KStars/Building_KStars"
"\"> &kstars; Git </ulink> verzija koda. Postoji nekoliko obavijesna datoteka "
"u distribuciji koje objašnjavaju neke od kodova podsustava. Ako vam je "
"potrebna ideja o tome što se radi o, pogledajte TODO datoteku. Možete "
"podnijeti peč za kstars-raz, i slobodno postavljati pitanja koja imate o "
"kodu kao i tamo."

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are not into coding, we can still use your help with i18n, docs, "
"AstroInfo articles, &URL; links, bug reports, and feature requests."
msgstr ""
"Ako niste za  kodiranje, još uvijek možete koristiti pomoć s i18n, "
"dokumente, AstroInfo članancima, &URL; linkovi, izvješća o pogreškama i "
"mogućnost zahtjeva."
